  "language": null,
  "rootCause": "Cauldron V4 tracked debt in two separate variables: elastic (the actual MIM token amount outstanding) and base (debt shares). Integer rounding in the borrow and repay functions caused a one-unit discrepancy per cycle. The attacker first flash-loaned 300,000 MIM from DegenBox to call repayForAll and individually repay every active borrower, zeroing the pool's elastic/base totals. A helper contract then executed 90 rapid borrow(1) / repay(1) loops; each cycle introduced a rounding error that decoupled elastic from base, eventually driving elastic to 0 while base remained non-zero. With the pool believing no debt was outstanding, the attacker deposited yvCurve-3Crypto collateral and borrowed the entire remaining MIM balance of the DegenBox. Vulnerable code snippet: Attack Tx: 0x26a83db7e28838dd9fee6fb7314ae58dcc6aee9a20bf224c386ff5e80f7e4cf2 Analysis: MIM Spell Exploit Analysis",
  "descriptions": [
    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs explorer",
      "text": "Cauldron V4 tracked debt in two separate variables: elastic (the actual MIM token amount outstanding) and base (debt shares). Integer rounding in the borrow and repay functions caused a one-unit discrepancy per cycle. The attacker first flash-loaned 300,000 MIM from DegenBox to call repayForAll and individually repay every active borrower, zeroing the pool's elastic/base totals. A helper contract then executed 90 rapid borrow(1) / repay(1) loops; each cycle introduced a rounding error that decoupled elastic from base, eventually driving elastic to 0 while base remained non-zero. With the pool believing no debt was outstanding, the attacker deposited yvCurve-3Crypto collateral and borrowed the entire remaining MIM balance of the DegenBox. Vulnerable code snippet: Attack Tx: 0x26a83db7e28838dd9fee6fb7314ae58dcc6aee9a20bf224c386ff5e80f7e4cf2 Analysis: MIM Spell Exploit Analysis"
    }
  ],
